# s4_ars_charge
#
# basis      s3 peak 1,198,664 kB; anon:[heap] 962.9 MB (78.4%, not a target); largest named object
#            heap:span.hpp:24:shark::span<shark::crypto::DCFBitKey>::span, 75.5 MB.
# identity   recv_dcfbit(n, bin): one span<DCFBitKey> of n keys (96 B each, named) plus three small
#            allocations per key (k, v_bit, v_tag_1): 1040 + 64 + 512 = 1616 B at bit width 64,
#            320 + 19 + 152 = 491 B at width 19, below the 64 KiB floor, in the brk heap.
#            75.5 MB / 96 B = 2 x 393,216 keys (two FFN truncations); 393,216 x (1616 + 491) B = 828.5 MB
#            against 962.9 MB unnamed. Named object = visible 8% of a 904 MB object.
# lever      charge the truncation in blocks of 98,304 = 128 x 768 (target granularity); truncations
#            at or below that width unchanged.
# protocol   loop inside lrs::call, run by all three parties (dealer charges identically). Fixed during
#            writing: eval's `Y = authenticated_reconstruct(...)` move-assign would rebind an unmanaged
#            view; now writes through Y. Gate byte-identical.
# impl_snapshot: src/bert_instrumented_s4_ars_charge.cpp patches/s4_stream_and_charge.diff
# Library patch provenance (checked 2026-09-29 in shark-s4_ars_charge.sif on PALMA; earlier this line
# named patches/filebuf_read_buffer.diff alone, without s4's lrs.cpp charge-chunk change).
# /root/extra.diff in the image: md5 10d293d53bd828ca8e9a74350089686a = impl/patches/s4_stream_and_charge.diff
# (filebuf_read_buffer.diff, md5 7d5c715e..., plus lrs_charge_chunk.diff); s3 image: 7d5c715e....
# lrs.cpp contains LRS_CHARGE (3 matches; 0 in the s3 image); binary md5 69332cd2c4af6add70878e938330297f
# = binary_md5.txt of every published run of this step.
# s1 to s3 plus this step's lever.
# pool_attacked: host
# object_attacked: shark::span<shark::crypto::DCFBitKey>
OMP_NUM_THREADS=4
